  "answer_text": "Unfortunately, the Indiana Pacers are **not** in the 2026 NBA Playoffs. The Indiana Pacers missed the playoffs for the first time since 2023.\n\nThis was largely due to the full-year absence of Tyrese Haliburton, who was sidelined with a torn Achilles tendon sustained in Game 7 of the 2025 NBA Finals. Key players including Aaron Nesmith, Obi Toppin, and Ben Sheppard also missed significant time due to injuries, which plagued Indiana's record.\n\nIt's worth noting that the Pacers were the defending Eastern Conference champions \u2014 the Thunder won their first NBA title by beating the Indiana Pacers in a seven-game Finals that went right down to the wire in 2025. The 2026 NBA Finals are currently being contested between the **New York Knicks** and the **San Antonio Spurs**.",
